#!/bin/bash
# Boat's `lux` (machines/tools: "Desktop and browser automation with demo
# recording") is Ascii's proprietary GUI agent, driven by their hosted Lux
# model. It is not published, so CrowdVM ships this pointer instead of it.
cat >&2 <<'MSG'
lux is not available on CrowdVM (it is Boat's proprietary desktop agent).
Use instead:
  drive the desktop    the `computer` MCP tools of the integrated agents (cua-driver),
                       or xdotool / wmctrl / scrot with DISPLAY=:0
  record a demo        ascii-record-desktop start demo.mp4; ...; ascii-record-desktop stop
  hand off a GUI task  crowdvm prompt <sandbox id> "<task>"  (from outside the sandbox)
MSG
exit 127
